 "summary": "No lesson was clean. Systemic exam errors across all eight lessons: the unit teaches a two-part 20 + 20 question that this board does not set, defines AO4 as context, tells students context earns marks in a section that assesses AO1, AO2 and AO4 only, and names the board in student-facing text; all 48 practice questions were relabelled to the single 40-mark source-based question with the house band ladder. On content, the biggest problem is an invented Irwin catchphrase, 'torture the evidence', on which L4 builds an entire fabricated 'double meaning' reading of the Holocaust scene; that scene was also misreported (Irwin credited with the boys' arguments, and Posner's Act 1 speech relocated into it). Nine further fabricated or misattributed quotations were replaced with verified lines, and factual errors on the setting, the Brief Encounter scene, Drummer Hodge and Philip Larkin were corrected. One cluster of unverifiable Headmaster quotations is recorded as a NOTE rather than edited.",
